This project includes BoringSSL, a fork of OpenSSL developed by
Google. The current master HEAD and the historical V4 freeze use
different BoringSSL versions:

### Current (master HEAD)

- **Version:** commit df821137838169360f82f94fd39cebe803c7c2d6 (2026-10-22)
- **Source:** https://github.com/google/boringssl
- **License:** Apache License, Version 2.0
- **Build:** NDK 26.1.10909125, Clang 17.0.2, CMake 3.22.1
- **Files:** `adb-engine/src/main/cpp/third_party/boringssl/`

### Historical (V4 freeze, AG consumer)

- **Version:** UNKNOWN (pre-2025-02-03 BoringSSL)
- **Source:** https://github.com/google/boringssl (exact commit unrecoverable)
- **License:** OpenSSL BSD + SSLeay BSD + ISC + MIT (pre-switch)
- **Build:** NDK r27, Clang 18.0.1, 2026-09-24
- **SHA-256:** `602A6D6C6DA1C5017A6C19C7EEE3F40C5653D200E2DA0B22B6238DA214F865D2`
- **Present in:** Git history (commit `a40387e`), freeze tag `AT.V4-CONSUMER-FREEZE-V1`, frozen AAR

The historical BoringSSL license text is preserved at:
`docs/legal/boringssl/HISTORICAL_BORINGSSL_LICENSE.md`

The historical BoringSSL compliance audit is at:
`docs/legal/boringssl/HISTORICAL_BORINGSSL_COMPLIANCE.md`

The original OpenSSL copyright notices (Eric Young, Tim Hudson, and
others) are preserved in the individual header file comments in both
versions.

